{"thought": "I have the full spec. Let me implement the function. Key points: split with splitlines, skip lines inside fenced code blocks, match ATX heading pattern with 1-6 hashes preceded by at most 3 spaces, title after space/tab, drop optional closing run of # preceded by space or whole title. Bare '#' is level-1 empty title.","action": {"tool": "edit_file", "args": {"path": "src/textkit/extract_headings.py", "old": "    raise NotImplementedError", "new": "    import re

    lines = markdown.splitlines()

    # Regex for an ATX heading line: up to 3 leading spaces, 1-6 '#', then
    # end-of-line or a space/tab before the title.
    heading_re = re.compile(r"^( {0,3})(#{1,6})(?:[ \t]+(.*))?$")

    results: List[Tuple[int, str]] = []

    in_fence = False
    fence_char = ""

    for line in lines:
        # Detect fence open/close: line starting (after <=3 spaces) with ``` or ~~~
        fence_match = re.match(r"^( {0,3})(```|~~~)", line)
        if fence_match:
            char = fence_match.group(2)[0]
            if not in_fence:
                in_fence = True
                fence_char = char
            elif char == fence_char:
                in_fence = False
                fence_char = ""
            continue

        if in_fence:
            continue

        m = heading_re.match(line)
        if not m:
            continue

        level = len(m.group(2))
        title = m.group(3)
        if title is None:
            title = ""
        else:
            title = title.strip()
            # Drop an optional closing run of '#' preceded by a space or the whole title.
            if title.endswith("#"):
                # whole title is a run of hashes
                if re.fullmatch(r"#+", title):
                    title = ""
                else:
                    # closing run preceded by a space
                    stripped = title.rstrip("#")
                    if stripped and stripped[-1] == " ":
                        title = stripped.strip()
        results.append((level, title))

    return results"}}, "messages": []}

